speaker danien brinkley says he's  already seen the other side at least  three times  he spoke to the i-team's george knapp  i have been dead so many times it's like  a comedy routine  okay i mean when you get to talking  about being dead george i got a down  pat in 1975 a macho former star  athlete and u.s marine named danien  brinkley a self-described brawler  and redneck had a life-changing  life-ending experience  when a bolt of lightning slammed through  a phone line and into his skull  it melted the foam it went into the side  of my head above my ear  it went down my spine it welded the  nails of the heels of my shoes to the  floor  it threw me up in the air i see the  ceiling it slams me back down  a ball of fire comes through the room  and blinds me  i am burning i am on fire i am paralyzed  brinkley says he left his body floated  along with the ambulance as it raced to  a hospital  and watched from above as doctors  declared him dead  28 minutes later he says he awoke in the  hospital morgue  during the interim his consciousness  traveled through a tunnel  where he encountered a spiritual being  of light and  underwent a grueling replay of his  entire life  then in a flash he was back in his  severely injured body  it took him two years to be able to walk  again he told  few people what had happened and not  even his family believed him  but in the same year as the lightning  bolt incident a georgia physician dr  raymond moody wrote a book life after  life and coined the term  near-death experience or nde dr moody in  his book were pilloried by medical  colleagues  and by 1977 moody was broke and  despondent and ready to quit  former bully danien brinkley met moody  and became his staunchest defender  in 1989 during open heart surgery  brinkley died again  and once again visited what he perceived  to be the afterlife  he wrote a book saved by the light which  became a runaway bestseller  skeptics and debunkers came after him  disputing  biographical details and arguing that  ndes happen because the brain  is dying not because people are visiting  heaven brinkley who later had yet  another nde during brain surgery says  he's happy to take on all comers  including religious leaders  about what happens to us when we die if  i didn't go to hell  in the last four journeys nobody's going  to hell  okay so when you learn you don't die  when you learn your spiritual being and  you're not going to go to hell  that's enough to inspire you to change  brinkley put his beliefs into action he  spent tens of thousands of hours at the  bedsides of the dying  personally witnessed more than two  thousand people as they passed on  and created a program called the  twilight brigade which works with the va  to try to ensure that no military  veteran should  die alone a defiant brinkley hobbled by  a lifetime of serious injuries  knows he's helped thousands of people  who are facing death  whether science or religion believe him  or not why i  do these talks george is because nobody  dies  it never happens it's not  a part of the nature of reality  it's not george knapp 8 news now  tomorrow we will put up the full  interview with danien brinkley on our  mystery wire website along with  related links as well as additional  materials
 

